+for one identified node and a complete assessment period. The optional
+`platform.operator_node_exclusions` map uses positive decimal Node ID strings
+and only `type: required_kernel_option_disabled` records. Each record requires
+`node_name`, `node_role`, `valid_from`, `valid_through`, `option`, `value`,
+`source` and `reason`; unknown fields are rejected. Identity and source/reason
+must be nonempty strings, timestamps must be valid and ordered, `value` must be
+`n`, and the CONFIG option must be declared `enabled` in `required_options`.
+This is a reviewed negative applicability claim, not a historical kernel build
+or event attestation and not an arbitrary result override.
